This version uses one recursive call for each row. The helper prints the stars in the current row, then the next call works on one fewer star.

```java
class Solution {
    public void pattern5(int n) {
        printRows(n);
    }

    private void printRows(int stars) {
        if (stars <= 0) {
            return;
        }

        for (int i = 0; i < stars; i++) {
            System.out.print("*");
        }
        System.out.println();

        printRows(stars - 1);
    }
}
```

