The base condition also handles zero and negative input by returning before printing anything. The input is not changed.

Time complexity: `O(n^2)` because all rows together contain a quadratic number of stars.

Space complexity: `O(n)` for the recursion stack.

The number of rows is `n`. The first row has `n` stars, and each next row has one fewer star. A pair of loops handles the rows and the stars in each row.

For example, when `n = 4`, the rows contain 4, 3, 2, and 1 stars.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    void pattern5(int n) {
        for (int row = n; row >= 1; row--) {
            for (int star = 1; star <= row; star++) {
                cout << "*";
            }
            cout << endl;
        }
    }
};
```

